items.body:
I am a solo developer in Germany. In the evenings I build LexyBooster, a German vocabulary app with spaced repetition ( https://lexybooster.com ). A month ago I stopped writing most of the code myself and set up a small "dark factory": a pipeline of AI agents that picks up GitHub issues, writes the code, runs the tests, reviews the pull request and merges it when every gate is green. 

 The setup is boring on purpose: 


 one Hetzner VPS (4 vCPU, 8 GB RAM, about 12.60 USD a month); 
 Archon runs the workflows, Paperclip keeps budgets and schedules, LiteLLM routes every call to the cheapest model that can do the job; 
 free models first (Groq, Cerebras), Gemini Flash-Lite when they are not enough, and a Claude subscription for planning and review; 
 every merge decision is made by a script
